==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|spécificité}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/spɛsɪˈfɪsɪti/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|specificities}}

# The state of being [[specific]] rather than [[general]].
# {{label|en|statistics}} The [[probability]], in a [[binary]] [[test]], of a true [[negative]] being correctly identified.
# {{label|en|medicine}} The extent to which a particular diagnostic test is specific for a given condition.

====Synonyms====
* [[specificness]] (much less common)

====Antonyms====
* [[genericity]]

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|statistics|binary probability}} [[sensitivity]]

